HLPDIST {
[1;36mTopic: Distress signals

Some ships, if attacked, will send a distress signal on a hyperspace frequency
throughout the galaxy. If you wish (and are in range), you can defend the ship
in distress by trying to take out its attacker. If you're successful, you will
earn an additional point bonus and the appreciation of those that you rescued.

Your ship's phasers are programmed to not damage a ship in distress (unless you
are the one attacking it). This way, you can fire on a ship in the same area
and not worry about hitting the ship in distress. If you want to override this
behavior, use the [1;37mLOCK[1;36m command on the ship in distress, you can then fire as
normal.
[1;37m} T GE help distress message

HLPNAVIG {
[1;36mTopic: Moving (Navigating)
All directional information in Galactic Empire functions on a 360 degree
compass and is strictly two dimensional. The major bearings are as follows:

       [1;37m315  0  45
          \ | /
           \|/
     270----*----90
           /|\
          / | \
       225 180 135[1;36m

BEARING -- Bearing is always used to indicate where a particular ship or planet
is in relation to you. It is relative to the direction you are facing and
expressed in a number from -179 to 180. If a object is bearing -90, it is to
the left of you, if 90 it is to the right of you, if 0 it is directly in front
of you, and if 180 it is directly behind you.

HEADING -- Heading is the relative direction of the other ship. It is used to
indicate when a ship is facing toward or away from you. A heading of 0 means
the ship is facing toward you, while a heading of 180 is away from you.

GALACTIC HEADING -- This is the absolute heading in the galaxy. A galactic
heading of 0 means you (or the other ship) is facing north up.[1;37m
} T GE help navigate message

HLPPLANT {
[1;36mTopic: Owning planets

In order to build up wealth, you must colonize planets and maintain them.
Planets are claimed by simply going into orbit around one and using the [1;37mADMIN[1;36m
command. You should be choosy at first about which planets you put a population
on, as surviving on a poor planet can be very difficult and require frequent
supply runs.

Planets are rated on two factors, resources and environment, with the following
categories: POOR, MARGINAL, GOOD, and VERY GOOD. The resources factor rates the
natural resources of the planet. A rating of good or very good will insure that
your population has plenty of natural resources to use in the establishment of
the colony, and the manufacture of goods. The environment factor rates the
hospitality of the planet and how difficult it will be for a colony to survive.
A rating of good, or very good, will insure that the majority of their efforts
go toward producing goods and not simply surviving.

Once you have claimed a planet, you need to establish a population on it. This
is done with the [1;37mTRANSFER[1;36m command to shuttle items from your ship to a planet.

Type [1;37mHELP PLANETS2[1;36m for more information on planets.
[1;37m} T GE help planets message

HLPPLAN2 {
[1;36mTopic: Owning planets (section 2)

It is a good idea to leave some additional items on a planet. They are:

FOOD -- If you fail to leave food on the planet you will find your men and
troops all dead when you return next time. It is a good idea to leave a case
for every 10 men & troops you have, and to make sure you produce enough so your
planet can sustain itself (see section 3).

TROOPS -- Troops are mercenaries, who produce nothing, but serve to defend your
planet from outside attacks and prevent domestic revolts. They must be fed
well, and will fight to the death when attacked.

FIGHTERS -- Fighters will defend your planet from both ground troop invasions
and fighter attacks. They provide a primary defense force for your planet.

ION CANNON -- This is a large defensive cannon which fire every few seconds on
any ship that attacks your planet, and is capable of destroying a ship in a
few shots. Only one ion cannon is active at a time, but it's wise to keep
additional on hand in case any are destroyed in an attack.

Type [1;37mHELP PLANETS3[1;36m for more information on planets.
[1;37m} T GE help planets2 message

HLPPLAN3 {
[1;36mTopic: Owning planets (section 3)

When a planet is first established, your colony will divide their efforts
between reproducing and growing food. You may wish to instruct the colony to
boost your planetary defenses or create weapons for your or your team's use.

Your colony will produce all the supplies you need for your ship if managed
properly. You can also choose to sell items to other commanders if you choose.
Any cash spent on goods from your planet goes into the planetary bank. Keeping
the planetary bank from going bankrupt will boost the production and maximum
capacity of your planet by 50 percent. Producing gold is another way to ensure
your planetary bank stays full.

If you wish to be selective in who can purchase from your planets, you can
establish a trade password for your planet and only those who know the password
can buy from you. This is also useful in establishing an alliance with other
players where you all would set your planets to the same password and agree on
the price to charge each other. Non-members will be excluded from trading with
your alliance.

Remember that the better your planet, the more attractive it is to marauders.
Nothing can take the place of a well-rounded defense system and frequent supply
runs. Leaving a planet unchecked for more than a few days may spell disaster
for your colony.  
[1;37m} T GE help planets3 message

HLPSTRAT {
[1;36mTopic: Game strategy

Your ship is equipped with nothing but a few flux pods when you first enter the
game, but you are not in any imminent danger as sector 0 0 is a neutral zone.

On Zygor you can purchase shield systems, phaser systems, missiles, torpedoes,
jammers, decoys, mines, and zippers. Note: some of these may not be available
or useful on some ship classes (see [1;37mHELP CLASS[1;36m for more info). You can also
purchase fighters and ion cannons for your planets. On Tahanian Station you can
purchase colonists (men), troops, and food.

Your first goal should be to colonize at least one planet to provide a source
for revenue you will need to expand your empire and keep your ships fully
stocked. To do this you should purchase men, troops, food, and some fighters.
Locate the best planet you can find and use [1;37mADMIN[1;36m to claim it.

An alternative, albeit somewhat immoral, strategy is to purchase weapons and
lie waiting for other ships to leave sector 0 0. When they do, mount an attack.
Upon destroying their ship, you will gain what remains of their supplies.

Remember, these are only a couple suggested strategies, and others are only
limited by your imagination.
[1;37m} T GE help strategy message

HLPBATTL {
[1;36mTopic: Battle strategy

The flexibility of Galactic Empire precludes an exhaustive discussion of all
the strategies involved in user-versus-user battling. Some suggestions are
simply put forth here to get you started.

When in a potential battle situation make sure your shields are up, and keep
moving. The easiest target is a ship with shields down, sitting still.

If you have incoming torpedoes, you can ditch them easily by making a jump to
light speed (provided you have warp drive). Missiles, however, can travel
through hyperspace; you can only shake them off by fleeing at high warp.

The more charge a missile carries, the more damage it does when it hits, but
heavily charged missiles travel more slowly. Missiles use energy as they
travel, and will eventually run out of charge and disappear if they don't hit
their target. Since the payload from a missile is mostly flux energy, shields
are incredibly effective at absorbing a missile blast.

Type [1;37mHELP BATTLE2[1;36m for more information on battling.
[1;37m} T GE help battle message

HLPBATT2 {
[1;36mTopic: Battle strategy (section 2)

If you have a cloaking system, use it sparingly as it consumes incredible
amounts of energy; it is most useful in covering a retreat.

Launching decoys does not guarantee that the incoming missiles or torpedoes
will be destroyed. Launching more decoys than incoming weapons increases the
chance of destroying an incoming weapon.

If a target goes to light speed, be prepared to make the jump with them and use
hyper-phasers as soon as you pass warp 1.

If you get hit with a hyper-phaser, immediately go into a series of high speed
turns as your opponent will have difficulty locating you. Go out of light speed
in another sector and immediately cloak as a last ditch effort to lose your
pursuers.

Type [1;37mHELP BATTLE3[1;36m for more information on battling.
[1;36m} T GE help battle 2 message

HLPBATT3 {
[1;36mTopic: Battle strategy (section 3)

Form alliances to help protect each other from marauders. Remember, two ships
are twice as powerful as one.

When you are under attack you cannot exit the game to avoid your attackers. If
you disconnect while you are under attack your ship will be destroyed.
Remember, "death before dishonor!"

If you are damaged, try to make it back to sector 0 0 or to any populated
planet where you can get your ship repaired with the [1;37mMAINTENANCE[1;36m command.
Remember, the cost for everything is much more expensive in Sector 0 0.

When you destroy another ship, you will get some of the goods that were on that
ship. This can be very helpful when you are running low.

Type [1;37mHELP BATTLE4[1;36m for more information on battling.
[1;37m} T GE help battle 3 message

HLPBATT4 {
[1;36mTopic: Battle strategy (section 4, planetary battles)

Planets can defend themselves with troops, fighters, and ion cannons. If you
have no troops or fighters, your planet can be easily overrun.

FIGHTERS are Nova-class battle fighters commanded by a fully automated tactical
computer. They have inboard and outboard photon cannons capable of powerful and
offensive and defensive attacks. However, due to galactic treaty, fighters
launched from a ship are not programmed to attack troops stationed on a planet.

TROOPS are trained mercenaries, and serve no other function than the defense of
(or attack on) a planet. They consume food, maintain their skills, and mostly
play cards, but when needed they will fight to the death.

ION CANNONS are very powerful fixed focus, ion-plasma transmitters, capable of
taking out a large ship with only a few strikes. When the planet comes under
attack, they will automatically locate the attacker's ship and commence firing.

When attacking a planet you are always at a disadvantage, as the local troops
and fighters are better supported and fresh. Knowing this, you should always
plan on commencing a battle with superior numbers. If the planet has fighters,
begin with a fighter attack. Clear out all fighters from the planet before
attempting to attack with troops. Remember, you will not take a planet so long
as 1 fighter or 1 squad of troops (5) exists on the planet.
[1;37m} T GE help battle 4 message

HLPCYBER {
[1;36mTopic: Cybertrons

Cybertrons are a race of automatons which command a class of ship manufactured
specifically for them, also called the Cybertron. Both pilot and ship function
as a single fighting unit, and they can be quite deadly.

Cybertrons have made massive improvements to their ships in the past few
decades, leading them to turn against the Sartens, with whom they once shared
an uneasy alliance. Cybertrons are now bent on the destruction of all organic
life from the galaxy, including the Sartens, Murdonians, and (presumably) you.

All Cybertrons are equipped with a pursuit capability to identify non-Cybertron
ships throughout the galaxy, and are capability of traversing the galaxy in
mere moments to reach a ship, at speeds far beyond warp as currently
understood. All attempts by the Galactic Command to reverse engineer this
technology have so far failed. A scan of a Cybertron ship traveling at this
pursuit speed will display "??.??" for speed.

The least powerful Cybertron is a Cybertron Interceptor, which can be
identified by its "1x" marking. The top cruising speed of a Cybertron
Interceptor is warp 8.0, and it is equipped only with phaser, shield, and
torpedo systems. As you destroy Cybertrons and upgrade to more powerful ships,
you will find more powerful classes of Cybertrons will be dispatched to
intercept you. It is up to you to discover the capabilities of these ships.
[1;37m} T GE help Cybertron message

HLPLYDO {
[1;36mTopic: Lydorians

Eight hundred years ago, the Lydorians and the Sartens fought a war that nearly
brought both powers to mutual destruction. However, when the Sartens finally
developed faster-than-light travel, the war effectively ended. The Lydorians
were offered a treaty with the Sartens ending all hostilities as long as the
Lydorians agreed to never develop hyperspace technology of their own. Facing
certain defeat, the Lydorians reluctantly agreed.

Today, this treaty is still in effect and the Lydorians have adopted a
pacifist, isolationist lifestyle. Some Lydorians operate garbage scows that
don't require warp drive, most choose not to interact with the rest of the
galaxy at all.

During the Cybertron-Sarten War, the Lydorians developed the Planetary
Transport vessel, capable of evacuating entire populations of planets out of
the path of destruction. When hostilities died down, the government of Lydoria
sold the design specifications to the Galactic Command. The Planetary Transport
is sold at Zygor today.
[1;37m} T GE help Lydorian message

HLPMURD {
[1;36mTopic: Murdonians

The Murdonians are one of the few powers in the galaxy to never get caught up
in full-scale war or galactic conquest. After acquiring warp capability several
hundred years ago, the Murdonian government eventually spun off their space
program into the Trans-Gal Corporation, serving the transportation needs of the
entire galaxy.

Today, the Trans-Gal Corporation moves tens of thousands of people and hundreds
of thousands of tons of equipment throughout the galaxy every day. While the
Murdonians possess no military force of their own, Trans-Gal vessels are
capable of self-defense to protect their passengers and cargo from Cybertrons
and other marauders.
[1;37m} T GE help Murdonians message

HLPSART {
[1;36mTopic: Sartens

Once a proud warrior race, and the dominant military power in the galaxy, the
Sarten Empire is in ruins after the Cybertron-Sarten War of 3274.

In the past thirty years, Cybertrons have greatly upgraded their fleet with
newer, more powerful ships, and quickly outclassed even the most powerful
Sarten Obliterators. The delicate balance of power that led the Sartens to
thrive even after the rise of the Cybertrons quickly deteroriated.

Sartens are now focused on transporting what remains of their kind out of the
path of Cybertron destruction. Most of their fleet is now comprised of
transport vessels, which will not attack anyone except for in self-defense.
They also control a handful of defense drones which will seek out Cybertrons
and anyone else who has threatened what remains of their empire.

While no longer a threat to the galaxy at large, many ship commanders have not
forgotten the terror that Sartens have wrought in the past. Whether you wish to
attack, ignore, or defend the Sartens is up to you, but be advised that they
will respond in kind.
[1;37m} T GE help Sartens message

HLPTRYK {
[1;36mTopic: Tryklons

The Tryklons are a nomadic species, and whether they are real or simply a
legend had been debated for many years. Several ship commanders have reported
approaching a unknown vessel, but being quickly thrown off course by an unknown
force, and returning to find no trace of the ship.

In 3277, a Vakory Survey Drone captured what are believed to be the first
visual scans of a Tryklon ship ever recorded. However, the drone mysteriously
vanished after transmitting its findings to the Vakory High Command.

Legend says the Tryklons were the first spacefaring race in the galaxy, possess
unknown and powerful technology, and are responsible for seeding the galaxy
with the wormholes that are commonly used today. However, Zygorian scientists
dismiss these claims.

One of the wormholes in the neutral zone was named the Tryklon Portal in honor
of these legends.
[1;37m} T GE help Tryklons message

HLPVAKO {
[1;36mTopic: Vakories

One hundred years ago, the Vakories believed they were alone in the galaxy,
until their fledgling space program led them to discover Sarten vessels in a
neighboring sector. Fearing hostility, the Vakories developed unmanned research
vessels to help them understand the giant galaxy that they now understood they
inhabited.

Today, the Vakory Survey Drone program is considered the leading scientific
research program in the galaxy. Vakory Survey Drones map the galaxy, study
spatial phenomena, and share their findings with Zygorian scientists and the
galaxy at large.

To this day, no Vakory citizen has ever left their home planet.
[1;37m} T GE help Vakories message

HLPZYGO {
[1;36mTopic: Zygorians

Zygor, in the heart of the galaxy, sector [1;34m0 0[1;36m, is the home of Zygorian people,
and also home to the headquarters of the Galactic Command, recognized as the
only interplanetary legal authority in the galaxy.

Zygor is also the leader in state-of-the-art weapons and ship hardware. Zygor
manufactures the various ships and the weapons they carry. It is also home of
the Galactic Monetary Reserve Fund, the only duly authorized financial
institution in the galaxy.

In 3250, the Galactic Command established the neutral zone, a perimeter around
sector 0 0 inside which no hostility is permitted. This policy is maintained by
the Enforcer Planet, home to a secret base capable of nullifying any weapons
fire detected within the sector.

While at Zygor, ship commanders may buy and sell goods, purchase new ships and
upgrades, and get their ships repaired. Also in the neutral zone is Tahanian
Station, a embarking station for colonists and mercenary soldiers, where you
can find men, troops, and food for your own planets.

Galactic Command Freighters are dispatched from Zygor to bring supplies to
planets throughout the galaxy. Any hostility towards these ships may result in
your being banned from conducting business in the neutral zone.
[1;37m} T GE help Zygorians message

HLPSCORE {
[1;36mTopic: Scoring

Scores are based upon the size of your empire and the number and class of kills
you have accumulated in ship-to-ship combat.  Each class of ship is worth a
different number of points.

Cybertron Scouts are worth 1000 points. More powerful Cybertrons are worth
more; you will have to destroy them to find how much.

Enter [1;37mHELP CLASS[1;36m to view the points awarded for destroying user ships.
Additionally, you are awarded a small percentage of the defeated player's score
in addition to the ship points.

Finally, when you destroy another player's ship, their score also goes down.
This means that you can actually knock players down on the top player list,
making it easier to overtake them (or pass them further).
[1;37m} T GE help scoring message

HLPWORM {
[1;36mTopic: Wormholes

Wormholes are fairly rare galactic anomalies caused by a paired spatial
singularity. In effect, they create a means of "leaping" across the galaxy to
another sector. To navigate through a wormhole you must carefully approach it
directly at about 1/4 impulse. You will be pulled into the wormhole and emerge
at the terminal sector. If you approach too fast, you will simply miss the
event horizon. If you approach too slow, you may oscillate between terminal
sectors.

Each time you pass through a wormhole, some damage to systems may occur.
Passing through a wormhole while severely damaged is not recommended. Wormholes
are usually bidirectional, but an even rarer form of one way wormhole has been
speculated to exist.
[1;37m} T GE help wormhole message

HLPNEB {
[1;36mTopic: Nebulas

Nebulas are sectors in the galaxy filled with ionized hydrogen and cosmic dust.
Inside a nebula, your ship's scanners will be extremely limited. Scanners will
only be able to work within a small radius around the ship in sector view and
all scanner functionality outside the nebula will be blocked.

A ship inside the nebula is also completely shielded from all scans from
outside the nebula. This means a nebula can be an effective place to hide, but
you won't have any idea what's going on outside of it.

Phaser fire is not affected by nebulas, and you can fire into and out of them
as you please. If you think someone's hiding in a nebula, that's certainly an
effective way to check.

Planets and wormholes can exist in a nebula just like any other sector, but
your scanners will not be able to locate them unless they're very close to you.
A high quality planet in a nebula can be very valuable, as it adds an extra
layer of security for your colony. If you own a planet in a nebula, your 
ship's systems will remember its location in sector scans.
[1;37m} T GE help nebula message

HLPUPG {
[1;36mTopic: Ship upgrades

Various upgrades for your ship's systems are available at Zygor. Each class of
ship has different upgrades that are applicable to that class of ship. The
prices for these upgrades also vary from class to class, with more powerful
ships generally requiring pricier upgrades.

To see what upgrades are available for your ship class, go to Zygor and enter
[1;37mNEW UPGRADE[1;36m. To purchase an upgrade, enter [1;37mNEW UPGRADE [1;32mx[1;36m, where [1;32mx[1;36m is the
number of the upgrade.

Upgrades are for the ship in which they are installed only, and they can't be
transferred or returned once installed. Be careful to not put a lot of money
into upgrading your ship only to carelessly lose it later.

Installed upgrades are shown in [1;37mREP UPG[1;36m. Upgraded ships will be shown with
[1;37m+[1;36m symbols added to the ship's class in scans.
[1;37m} T GE help upgrade message

HLPADM {
[1;36mThe [1;37mADMIN[1;36m command permits you to claim and administer a planet once in orbit.
If you already own this planet, you can perform several planetary maintenance
functions from the planet administration menu.

Option 1 is an accounting report, which shows you the quantity of items on your
planet, the sale price you have set for each item, the percentage of effort
that your colonists have been instructed to put into the production of each
item, and the balance of your planetary and tax banks.

Option 2 allows you to collect money from the tax bank.

Option 3 is used to adjust the sale price and production rate of each item.

Option 4 will allow you to rename your planet.

Option 5 is for adjusting the planet's tax rate.

Option 6 is for setting a trade password; only users that know this password
will be able to purchase goods or request maintenance.

Option 7 sets a beacon message that will be broadcast to all ships that are
near your planet and not in hyperspace.
[1;37m} T GE help admin message

HLPABA {
[1;36mThe [1;37mABANDON[1;36m command will release ownership of a planet previously claimed. You
must be in orbit around the planet to be abandoned.
[1;37m} T GE help abandon message

HLPABO {
[1;36mThe [1;37mABORT[1;36m command will abort a self-destruct countdown and prevent the
destruction of your ship.
[1;37m} T GE help abort message

