HLPORB {
[1;36mThe [1;37mORBIT[1;36m command is used to orbit a given planet. You must be traveling at
impulse or at a dead stop. If you are traveling at impulse, issuing the command
will stop the impulse engines.

Issue the command as follows:

[1;37m  orbit [1;32m[planet number]
[1;36m
You must be within 250 subsectors of a planet to establish an orbit.
[1;37m} T GE help orbit message

HLPPHA {
[1;36mThe [1;37mPHASER[1;36m command fires your ship's phasers in a given direction with a given
beam spread. The narrowest and most powerful spread is 0, whereas 5 covers the
widest range but is the least powerful. Wider beams can be useful when an
opponent is cloaked but you have a general idea of where they are, or when they
are moving quickly. If you do not specify a spread, a default of 1 is assumed.

Issue the command as follows:

  [1;37mphaser [1;32m[direction] [spread][1;37m

  [1;32mdirection[1;36m = the heading at which to fire the phasers, usually the bearing
              of another ship given in the "scan sh" command.

Examples: [1;37mphaser -15     [1;36mfire 15 degrees off port, focus 1.
          [1;37mpha 4 2        [1;36mfire 4 degrees off starboard, focus 2.
          [1;37mphaser 180 5   [1;36mfire directly behind, focus 5.

Phasers are programmed to avoid damaging ships in distress (unless you're the
one who attacked them first) or your teammates. To override this behavior, use
the [1;37mLOCK[1;36m command on the ship you're targeting first.

If you are traveling at warp speed, the hyper-phasers will be used instead. For
more information on hyper-phasers, see [1;37mHELP HYPER[1;36m.
[1;37m} T GE help phaser message

HLPPLA {
[1;36mThe [1;37mPLANET[1;36m command shows a list of planets in your empire.
[1;37m} T GE help planet message

HLPPRI {
[1;36mUse the [1;37mPRICE[1;36m command to determine the price of items for sale at a planet. You
must be orbiting a planet that is willing to sell you items.

Issue the command as follows:

[1;37m  price [1;32m[amount] [item]

  amount[1;36m = the amount you want priced

  [1;32mitem[1;36m:
    [1;37mmen[1;36m = price of men          [1;37mfig[1;36m = price of fighters
    [1;37mtro[1;36m = price of troops       [1;37mdec[1;36m = price of decoys
    [1;37mmis[1;36m = price of missiles     [1;37mmin[1;36m = price of mines
    [1;37mtor[1;36m = price of torpedoes    [1;37mjam[1;36m = price of jammers
    [1;37mion[1;36m = price of ion cannons  [1;37mzip[1;36m = price of zippers
    [1;37mflu[1;36m = price of flux pods    [1;37mgol[1;36m = price of gold
    [1;37mfoo[1;36m = price of food         [1;37mspy[1;36m = price of spies
[1;37m} T GE help price message

HLPREN {
[1;36mThe [1;37mRENAME[1;36m command will change the name assigned to your ship. Issue the
command as follows:

[1;37m  rename [1;32m[new ship name]

[1;36mYour ship name can be up to 19 characters long. Ship names are optional; to
clear your ship name simply enter [1;37mRENAME[1;36m.
[1;37m} T GE help rename message

HLPREP {
[1;36mThe [1;37mREPORT[1;36m command gives you status information on navigation, ship systems,
inventory, accounting, deployed ordnance, and installed upgrades. Issue the
command as follows:

  [1;37mreport [1;32m[[1;37mnav[1;32m/[1;37msys[1;32m/[1;37minv[1;32m/[1;37macc[1;32m/[1;37mord[1;32m/[1;37mupg[1;32m]

[1;36mExamples: [1;37mreport nav [1;36m produces a navigational report
          [1;37mreport sys [1;36m produces a systems report
          [1;37mreport inv [1;36m produces an inventory report
          [1;37mrep acc    [1;36m produces an accounting report
          [1;37mrep ord    [1;36m produces an ordnance report
          [1;37mrep upg    [1;36m produces an upgrade report
[1;37m} T GE help report message

HLPROS {
[1;36mThe [1;37mROSTER[1;36m command will display the top players roster. Your current ranking
number will also be displayed. Players that have yet to score any points will
not be displayed unless you specify [1;37mall[1;36m.

Issue the command as follows:

  [1;37mroster [1;32m[[1;37mall[1;32m]

[1;36mExamples: [1;37mroster [1;36mdisplays the top players
          [1;37mroster all [1;36mdisplays all players
[1;37m} T GE help roster message

HLPROT {
[1;36mThe [1;37mROTATE[1;36m command will cause the directional thrusters to rotate the ship a
specified number of degrees, or to a specified heading. If you specify an
absolute heading, the ship will automatically turn in the direction which
causes the shortest arc to arrive at the given heading. Issue the command as
follows:

[1;37m  rotate [1;32m[degrees]
[1;36m      or
[1;37m  rotate @[1;32m[heading]

[1;32m  degrees [1;36m= degrees to rotate to port (negative) or starboard (positive)
[1;32m  heading [1;36m= the absolute direction regardless of your current heading

  examples: [1;37mrotate 5   [1;36mturns the ship 5 degrees to the starboard (right)
            [1;37mrotate -5  [1;36mturns the ship 5 degrees to the port (left)
            [1;37mrot @5     [1;36mturns the ship to 5 degrees absolute
[1;37m} T GE help rotate message

HLPSET {
[1;36mThe [1;37mSET[1;36m command lets you set user-configurable options. Issue the command as
follows:

[1;37m  set [1;32m[option/[1;37m?[1;32m] [setting]
[1;36m
  [1;32moptions[1;36m:
[1;37m    scan [1;36m-- change SCAN SE/RA display
[1;37m       simple       [1;36m-- display maps only
[1;37m       full         [1;36m-- display maps with list of ships or planets
[1;37m       fullnames    [1;36m-- include ship names in list on second line
[1;37m       fullextra    [1;36m-- include more than 8 ships if necessary
[1;37m       nomap        [1;36m-- do not display map, text only

[1;37m    display [1;36m-- adjust messages shown
[1;36mEnter [1;37mHELP SET2[1;36m for more information on display filters.

[1;36mEnter [1;37mSET ?[1;36m to show a list of options and their current settings.

Examples:
[1;37m  set scan fullnames
  set display cybs off
  set ?     
} T GE help set message

HLPSET2 {
The type of messages displayed can be filtered with the [1;37mSET DISPLAY[1;36m command:

[1;37mcybs (off / approach / battle / on)
[1;36m  OFF -- show no Cybertron hails
  APPROACH -- only show hails from Cybertron tracking you as they approach
  BATTLE -- only show battle messages (includes APPROACH)
  ON -- show all Cybertron hails, including taunts
[1;37mdistress (off / on)
[1;36m  show distress messages from non-Cybertron ships
[1;37mbeacon (off / on)
[1;36m  show beacon messages from ships and planets
[1;37mhail (off / on)
[1;36m  show hailing messages from users (SEND ALL)
[1;37mentry (off / reduced / on)
[1;36m  OFF -- show no entry/exit messages
  REDUCED -- show messages immediately if player is in your scan range,
    otherwise only show if player has stayed in game for a while
  ON -- show all entry/exit messages
[1;37mship (off / on)
[1;36m  show non-critical ship functions (e.g. flux reload, sector change)

Examples:
[1;37m  set display hail on
  set display cybs off

[1;37m} T GE help set2 message

HLPSCA {
[1;36mThe [1;37mSCAN[1;36m command displays information from your ship's tactical scanners. Issue
the command as follows:

[1;37m  scan [1;32m[type] [ship letter/planet number/range]

[1;32mtype[1;36m:
  [1;37msh[1;36m = ship scan showing detail on [1;32mship letter
  [1;37mpl[1;36m = planet scan showing detail on [1;32mplanet number
  [1;37mse[1;36m = sector scan showing the ships, planets, and mines in this sector
  [1;37mra[1;36m = close range scan showing ships and mines
     [1;32mrange 1 to 9[1;36m can be specified, with 9 being full range, and the rest
     shrinking quadratically. Alternatively, [1;32mh[1;36m can be specified for half range,
     and [1;32mq[1;36m for one quarter range.
  [1;37mlo[1;36m = long range scan (10x) showing ships
     [1;32mh[1;36m can be specified for half range, and [1;32mq[1;36m for one quarter range.

[1;36mExamples: [1;37mscan se            scan sh a
          scan sh @          scan pl 1
          sca ra             sca ra 4
          sca lo             sca lo q

[1;36mSee the [1;37mSET[1;36m command for additional configuration options for [1;37mSCAN[1;36m.[1;37m
} T GE help scan message

HLPSEL {
[1;36mUse the [1;37mSELL[1;36m command to sell items to Zygor. The Galactic Command will charge a
small transfer tax on each transaction.

Issue the command as follows:

[1;37m  sell [1;32m[[1;37mall[1;32m/amount] [item]

  amount[1;36m = the amount you want to sell (or [1;37mall[1;36m to sell all onboard)

  [1;32mitem[1;36m:
[1;37m    men[1;36m = sell men          [1;37mfig[1;36m = sell fighters
[1;37m    tro[1;36m = sell troops       [1;37mdec[1;36m = sell decoys
[1;37m    mis[1;36m = sell missiles     [1;37mmin[1;36m = sell mines
[1;37m    tor[1;36m = sell torpedoes    [1;37mjam[1;36m = sell jammers
[1;37m    ion[1;36m = sell ion cannons  [1;37mzip[1;36m = sell zippers
[1;37m    flu[1;36m = sell flux pods    [1;37mgol[1;36m = sell gold
